        <section id="kanban"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Kanban
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Kanban was developed (with LEAN methodology) by an engineer for Toyota in the 1940s in Japan. It was predominately used in ‘just-in-time’ manufacturing.  Kanban came to the attention of the software industry and is nowadays used in the Agile methodology.</p>
<p>It is a visual system and the flow of work is managed from using a Kanban project board.  Often these same types of project boards are used in Agile and Scrum methodology.  In its simplest form there are three columns which are labelled: To Do, In Progress, and Done.</p>
<p>The objective of Kanban is to simplify planning, manage work and inventory, and increase productivity and efficiency.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s1_p3_image3.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
