        <section id="waterfall-project-management" >
          
            <h2>Waterfall Project Management</h2>
              <p>The waterfall project management approach emphasises a linear approach from the beginning to the end of a project. It flows like a waterfall through all phases of a project with each phase wrapping up before the next phase begins. It is often used by engineers and is front loaded relying on careful planning, detailed documentation, and consecutive execution.</p>
<p>It follows a chronological process and works on fixed dates, requirements, and outcomes.</p>
<p><img src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u1_s1_p4_wide_image_wf.svg" alt=""></p>

          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
